    "sections": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Night of the Demons epitomizes the wild, practical effects-driven horror of the late 1980s. Director Kevin Tenney crafted this Halloween party-gone-wrong cult classic during the peak of rubber monster suits and elaborate makeup effects. Like <a href=\"/movie/764\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"764\">The Evil Dead</a> (1981) and <a href=\"/movie/1694\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1694\">Re-Animator</a> (1985), it prioritizes outrageous demon transformations and dark humor over serious scares. The Hull House setting - an abandoned funeral parlor with a violent history - follows the \"teens in a haunted location\" template popularized by <a href=\"/movie/28377\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"28377\">Hell Night</a> (1981) and <a href=\"/movie/11415\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"11415\">House</a> (1985)."
      },
      {
