      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film's standout demon makeup by Steve Johnson deserves special recognition. Johnson had just come off <a href=\"/movie/6978\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"6978\">Big Trouble in Little China</a> (1986) and would go on to create effects for <a href=\"/movie/9348\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"9348\">Species</a> (1995). His work on Angela's demon transformation rivals the practical effects achievements of Rob Bottin in <a href=\"/movie/1091\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1091\">The Thing</a> (1982) and Rick Baker in <a href=\"/movie/814\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"814\">An American Werewolf in London</a> (1981). The lipstick scene became instantly iconic, referenced in horror films for decades after."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Scream queen Linnea Quigley, fresh off her career-defining role in <a href=\"/movie/10925\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"10925\">Return of the Living Dead</a> (1985), brings her signature punk attitude as Suzanne. The film follows the era's \"party horror\" trend seen in <a href=\"/movie/18462\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"18462\">Night of the Comet</a> (1984) and <a href=\"/movie/15762\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"15762\">Night of the Creeps</a> (1986), where teenage revelry turns to terror. The synthesizer score by Dennis Michael Tenney perfectly captures the 1980s horror atmosphere. SUBHEAD: Legacy and Influence"
      },
      {
